Cell["Basic Examples", "Subsection",
 Editable->True,
 TaggingRules->{},
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",
 CellID->904125756,ExpressionUUID->"8ad9d452-2e30-4456-a46b-e0afaf4735f7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Left contraction is a kind of inner product of multivectors a and b.  If \
grade(a) > grade(b) the result is multivector of grade(a) - grade(b) and zero \
otherwise. The StandardForm notation is \[LeftContract] (unicode char \\ \
:0x23A6). For input use keyboard alias \[EscapeKey]il\[EscapeKey] (memorize \
as \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 StyleBox["i",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 "nner ",
 StyleBox["l",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 "eft\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]).  UnicodeSymbols.tr defines the following \
operation precedences: NonCommutativeMultiply (**, highest), Times (*, \
Space), RightContract (\[RightContract]), LeftContract (\[LeftContract]), \
InnerProduct (\[InnerProduct]), CommutativeProduct (\[CommutativeProduct]), \
OuterProduct (\[OuterProduct]), GeometricProduct(\[GeometricProduct]), Plus \
(lowest). To demonstrate the action let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s define some basis \
and two general multivectors ",
 StyleBox["mva", "CodeText"],
