Cell[TextData[{
 "It is easy to remember that the vertical bar indicates the grade from which \
we subtract. In the first case 3\[LeftContract]\[DoubleStruckE][1]  we \
subtract from  grade 1 (vector) the grade 0 (scalar). Therefore the result is \
not zero. For the ",
 ButtonBox["RightContract",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{"RightContract.nb", None},
  ButtonNote->"RightContract"],
 StyleBox["\[MediumSpace]", "InlineSeparator"],
 " the  requirement is opposite."
}], "Text",
 Editable->True,
 TaggingRules->{},
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.954599763647778*^9, 3.9545997702428703`*^9}, {
  3.9580249314074163`*^9, 3.95802496582027*^9}, {3.9580250379104548`*^9, 
